# tally 2.2.1 (#233, 233.7; #235, 235.6), L §8.4's RUN-NONE row, `<x>[k] is none here: …`, and L §8.1: "with the item
# and keys each came from": fee[2026-02] is none in arithmetic under a binding (n), and flows of pay[m].cash before the
# run's start names pay[2026-01].cash (pr). tally 2.2 printed `a value is none here: arithmetic` and `pay[m].cash`.
=== nm.tally
model nm
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input rent[m in months]: money PLN
input fee[m in months]: money PLN
input lvl: num
move pay[m in months]: transfers
  on start_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to world amount rent[m]
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026-01
  known 2026-01-01
  rent = 100.00 PLN "s"
  fee = 5.00 PLN "s"
version v3
  cite s
  governs 2026-03..
  known 2026-01-01
  rent = 100.00 PLN "s"
version v2
  cite s
  governs 2026-02
  known 2026-01-01
  rent = ?"rent for February?" "s"
  fee = none "s"
ask b: sum(rent[m] for m in [2026-01, 2026-02, 2026-03])
ask c: flows(konto, 2026-01 .. 2026-03)
ask n: fee[m] + 1.00 PLN for m in [2026-01, 2026-02]
ask pr: flows(pay[m].cash, 2025-12-01 .. 2026-01-31) for m in [2026-01]
=== expect n pr b
n (m = 2026-01): 6.00 PLN
  cut 2026-01-01
n (m = 2026-02): refused: RUN-NONE fee[2026-02] is none here: arithmetic
  cut 2026-01-01
pr (m = 2026-01): ?"before the run's start" (pay[2026-01].cash)
  cut 2026-01-01
b: ?"rent for February?" (rent[2026-02])
  held: rent[2026-03] = 100.00 PLN (v3), read for 2026-03
  cut 2026-01-01
warning: WARN-UNREAD input lvl is read by nothing
